findings.citation_text:
750.100 - Several food items not allowed at the facility due to low risk permit were observed. The foods included, but were not necessarily limited to, the following:
A) BASEMENT: (grocery sack in cooler) 1. sour cream, 2. mayo, 3. butter, and 4. mustard; 
B) WALKIN COOLER: 1. soup in plastic ice cream tub & 2. mayo; 
C) CABINET IN BACK HALLWAY ABOVE MOP SINK: 1. various seasonings, 2. jars of beef base, 3. au jus gravy mix, & 4. onion dip mix.
Owner was told by Director of Environmental Health at 11/21/13 inspection that all foods were to be removed immediately and food service must stop. Owner noted he would comply at the time. The above items remain to be removed from the premises. Bartenders stated only popcorn has been served since the November inspection, and the equipment observed on-site is not used to make or serve food. 
**All of the abovementioned foods and any other products associated with food service must be removed from the facility. All equipment used for food service must be removed. The only foods that may remain on-site for service are frozen pizzas (to be cooked in a pizza oven inside the building), popping corn/associated supplies, and packaged snacks for the vending machine.**

findings.comment:
750.1350c - Several unused and/or unnecessary items were observed at the facility. Items included, but were not necessarily limited to, the following:
A) BAR: 1. roasting pans, 2. commercial slicer, 3. broken popcorn maker and poker machine (under table holding new popcorn maker);
B) APPLIANCES OUTSIDE: 1. two freezers, 2. fridge freezer unit, 3. washer & dryer;
C) OUTSIDE/UNDER LEAN-TO: 1. restaurant equipment and other items outside under lean-to on south side of building & 2. junk along the fence on the west end of the property;
D) BASEMENT: 1. stove, 2. cooler, & 3. various pieces of equipment, clothing and other junk. 
Remove all unnecessary items from the premises, including those that may have been overlooked and thus not mentioned in the above list. Only articles necessary for the operation and maintenance of the food service establishment shall be stored at the facility.
***CORRECT BY DATE TO BE DETERMINED AT COMPLIANCE CONFERENCE***
